WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.810
A practical Cyber Kill Chain routine starts with scope and purpose.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.860
Decide whether the team is reviewing an incident, planning detections,

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.735
evaluating controls, preparing an exercise, or summarizing intelligence.

00:00:10.735 --> 00:00:14.780
Then collect evidence and place observed behavior into the stage that best fits.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.295
Use careful language: observed, suspected, inferred,

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:19.414
and unknown should not mean the same thing.

00:00:19.414 --> 00:00:22.660
Record confidence and assumptions so later readers understand how conclusions were

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.180
reached.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.260
For each stage, ask what could detect, deny, disrupt, degrade, deceive,

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.047
or contain the activity.

00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:32.560
Look for telemetry gaps, prevention gaps, response gaps, and recovery gaps.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.980
Translate those gaps into improvements with owners: a new log source, a refined alert,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.560
a hardened exposed service, a tested containment path, a clearer playbook,

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.640
or a better executive summary.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.840
The routine should produce decisions, not just labels.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.800
It should help defenders communicate what happened, what evidence supports the assessment,

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.480
what risk remains,

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:50.440
and what will be improved.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.720
The core lesson is simple:

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.295
the Cyber Kill Chain is valuable when it turns intrusion progression into practical

00:00:55.295 --> 00:00:56.800
defensive action.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.612
Use the routine after the incident as well.

00:00:58.612 --> 00:01:02.150
Revisit the mapped stages, compare expected evidence to actual evidence,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.460
and ask where the team depended on luck or manual

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:04.960
effort.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.980
Those observations can become durable improvements to detections, controls, playbooks,

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.400
exercises, and reporting.
